22c9|v|To cover with a tilt, or awning. ; To incline; to tip; to raise one end of for discharging liquor; as, to tilt a barrel. ; To point or thrust, as a lance. ; To point or thrust a weapon at. ; To hammer or forge with a tilt hammer; as, to tilt steel in order to render it more ductile. ; To run or ride, and thrust with a lance; to practice the military game or exercise of thrusting with a lance, as a combatant on horseback; to joust; also, figuratively, to engage in any combat or movement resembling that of horsemen tilting with lances. ; To lean; to fall partly over; to tip.	o:269d,59,6;t1b,57,4;m2s,48,2;5zo,35,3;1ul9,31,1;5zk,28,1;22xr,24,5~269d,59,6;22xr,24,5;t1b,57,4;5zo,35,3;m2s,48,2;1ul9,31,1;5zk,28,1	s:5tf,46,2;1ul9,31,1;33s,20,4;225i,16,2;6r5,10,1~33s,20,4;225i,16,2;5tf,46,2;1ul9,31,1;6r5,10,1	D:5zk,48,4;1vcq,26,9;t15,10,3~1vcq,26,9;5zk,48,4;t15,10,3
